iokit: force the iOS C++ vtable layout under KEBAB

APPLE_KEXT_VTABLE_PADDING is 1 whenever XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX is defined, and this
port builds against the macOS SDK, so every OSMetaClassDeclareReservedUnused()
declaration became a real vtable slot: __ZTV9IOService is 274 slots here against
170 in the iOS 16.7.16 donor.

That is not a size difference, it is an offset difference.  A prelinked C++ kext
lays out its vtable for a 170-slot base while the kernel dispatches through a
274-slot one, so every virtual call from kext code lands on the wrong method --
IOStorageFamily's IOBlockStorageDriver would read reportBlockSize() out of a
reserved slot -- and no prelinked C++ kext can run.

Force the padding to 0 under KEBAB and keep XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX, which the SDK
headers still need.  Measured after the change: __ZTV9IOService is 170 slots,
matching the donor.

The reserved declarations expand to nothing with the padding off, so the export
lists that name those symbols have to change with it.  That is the next patch,
and it is not optional.

diff --git a/libkern/libkern/c++/OSMetaClass.h b/libkern/libkern/c++/OSMetaClass.h
index 78315a2..f4e3b71 100644
--- a/libkern/libkern/c++/OSMetaClass.h
+++ b/libkern/libkern/c++/OSMetaClass.h
@@ -162,11 +162,20 @@ class OSInterface
 
 #ifdef XNU_KERNEL_PRIVATE
 
-#if !XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX
+/*
+ * KEBAB is an iOS ABI port.  The prelinked kexts are iOS builds, where this is
+ * 0, but XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX is defined because the kernel is built against the
+ * macOS SDK, so every OSMetaClassDeclareReservedUnused() became a real vtable
+ * slot: IOService had 274 slots against the donor's 170.  A prelinked C++ kext
+ * then lays out its vtable for a 170-slot base while the kernel dispatches
+ * through a 274-slot one, and every virtual call lands on the wrong method.
+ * Keep XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX for the SDK headers, but match the iOS layout.
+ */
+#if defined(KEBAB) || !XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX
 #define APPLE_KEXT_VTABLE_PADDING   0
-#else /* !XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX */
+#else /* defined(KEBAB) || !XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX */
 #define APPLE_KEXT_VTABLE_PADDING   1
-#endif /* !XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX */
+#endif /* defined(KEBAB) || !XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX */
 
 #else /* XNU_KERNEL_PRIVATE */
 
